#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:11
msgid ""
"To customize this page, you can copy the core_modules/home directory to /"
"modules, but do not delete the original core_modules/home directory. You can "
"then make your modifications. You can delete parts of the copied directory, "
"such as Controller, Model, View, etc., where you are not making any changes. "
"This same logic applies to other resources like JavaScript (JS) and "
"Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) files. The /modules folder is the place for "
"your own modules or for customized versions of core modules."
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:12
msgid "Modular Customization"
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:13
msgid ""
"Only the files you want to modify should be saved within the /modules "
"directory, and they must be in the exact same path as they are in the "
"core_modules directory. This \"mirroring\" path ensures your customized "
"files seamlessly override the originals."
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:14
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:16
msgid ""
"If you only want to change the header and footer in /modules/inc, you just "
"need to copy those files from core_modules/inc and modify them. There's no "
"need to copy the entire main module."
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:17
msgid ""
"If you are changing a View component, it's enough to copy and modify only "
"the View of the desired module. The same applies to Model and all other "
"parts."
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:18
msgid ""
"Should the inc/header be changed only for this copied module, create a "
"header file in view/inc and also copy the corresponding controller. In the "
"controller, you must adjust the header's path, for example, from /inc/header "
"to inc/header (note the leading slash /). The header will then be loaded "
"from <module>/view/inc/header."
msgstr ""

#: /home/chris/NetBeansProjects/cevian/core_modules/home/view/home.php:19
